    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40798" root="هأ" body-key="h">
    
      R. Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَأْهَأَ بِالإِبِلِ</span></b> , (El-Umawee, S, K,) inf. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هِيهَآءٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَأْهَآءٌ</span>, (K,) the latter extr., (TA,) [see
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظَأْظَأَ</span>,] <i>He called the camels to food,</i> or <i>provender,
by the cry</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هِئْ هِئْ</span>: (S, K:) or he <i>chid</i> them,
(<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَجَرَهَا</span>), by the cry <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَأْهَأْ</span>. (K.) [See also arts.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جأ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جيأ</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَأْهَأَ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَأْهَآءٌ</span>, <i>He chid</i> a dog.
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <i>He called</i> a dog. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَأْهَأَ</span>, inf.
n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَأْهَآءٌ</span>, <i>He laughed loud and long:</i> [a word imitative of the sound]. (K, TA.)

